---
description: |
  Parses an ISC BIND `named` message body.

  The first field holds the raw message body, not the full Syslog envelope, and
  the second receives the structured BIND event:

  ```tql
  named::parse message, named
  ```

  The parser leaves the input field unchanged. It does not add a timestamp or
  provenance because those belong to the carrier around the message.
args:
  positional:
    - name: log
      description: The field holding the raw BIND named message body.
      type: field
    - name: named
      description: The field that receives the structured BIND named event.
      type: field
---

// The parser helpers use `_raw` as private scratch state. The public parser
// removes it before returning because only the caller can choose provenance.
$named = {_raw: $log.string()}
if $named._raw == null {
  @name = "named.parser_error"
  $named = {
    category: "parser",
    template: "missing_message",
    parser: {
      warning: "missing required input field",
      field: "message",
    },
  }
} else {
  // Parsers are probes: each leaves $named unchanged on no match.
  named::parsers::client event=$named
  if $named.category? == null {
    named::parsers::fallback event=$named
  }
  drop $named._raw
}
